module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.pipe_into_a_declared_function_resolves_as_a_method

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { BelowCeiling, FoundOnRung, RecurringFailureMode, RungRead }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { Mitigatable, StructurallyGuaranteed }
import gunbc.rung_climb { ClimbableButUnbuilt }

data pipe_into_a_declared_function_resolves_as_a_method: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "pipe_into_a_declared_function_resolves_as_a_method" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungRead { found_at: FoundOnRung { rung: Mitigatable }, standing: BelowCeiling { current: FoundOnRung { rung: Mitigatable }, ceiling: StructurallyGuaranteed, blocker: ClimbableButUnbuilt, trigger_capability: "the seed's resolver binds `xs |> f(args)` to an imported declared function f by declaration, with the piped value as f's first parameter, exactly as it binds a primitive or host-registered head -- executed check = a piped call into a modeled std.algebra declaration (list_sort_by_key with named key: and order:) resolves and returns the same list as the direct call" } },

  receipts: [
    "the seed resolves `xs |> f(..)` as a METHOD call on the receiver type, so a pipe into an imported, declared, modeled function refuses at resolve: `[\"b\", \"c\", \"a\"] |> list_sort_by_key(key: s => s, order: string_total_order())` fails with \"method 'list_sort_by_key' not found on receiver type 'Container(List,Primitive(String))'\" (probe module test.claim.sort_by_wave_pipe_probe, gunbc run on main 2026-10-24, sunny-bee-153). The same pipe binds when the head is a primitive or host-registered name (`acc |> list_push(b)` resolves throughout dag/extdeps/cloud/gcp/iam.dag), so the pipe's meaning depends on how the head is realized, not on what it declares.",

    "HARM: a name that leaves the ambient table for a modeled home cannot keep its pipe spelling, so each wave rewrites a piped site to the direct call (v2.workflow.roster_import_sweep roster_rename_pipe_edit, the RenameHead pipe form: `lhs |> f(a)` becomes `home(label0: lhs, label1: a)`, its operand bytes kept in place), and an author who pipes into a declared function gets a method-lookup refusal that names the wrong cause. ATTAINABLE CEILING: structurally guaranteed: a pipe is sugar for a call with the left operand as the first argument, so resolving it by the callee's declaration makes the refusal unwritable for every declared function. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, at capability grain: the seed's pipe resolution binds an imported declared function by declaration. Restoring the pipe form at the sort_by wave's sites is retired by that trigger.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
